$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The 4-pentenals 3a-h, PdCl2 (10 mol%), and
CuCl2 (10 mol%) were dissolved in aqueous DME (1:9) and stirred under an
oxygen atmosphere for 2-3 h. When the reaction was observed to be
complete, normal aqueous extractive work-up gave the ketoaldehydes 4a-h
in 71-84% yield. Compound 4e. viscous liquid, yield 71% IR [cm-1]
(neat/nujol): 2705.6, 1718.1, 1706.2; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ J (Hz): 0.91-1.02
(m, 6 H, 2 × CH3), 1.3-1.43 (m, 4 H, 2 × CH3- CH2-), 1.5-1.6 (m, 4 H, 2 ×
CH3CH2CH2), 2.11 (s, 3 H, CH3-C=O), 2.69 (d, 1 H, J = 17.1 Hz, O=C-CH2),
2.81 (d, 1 H, J = 17.1 Hz, O=CCH2), 9.57 (s, 1 H, -CHO); 13C NMR (CDCl3)
δ : 13.8 (-CH2CH3), 17.6 (-CH2CH3), 26.2 (CH3-C=O), 33.1 (-CH2CH2CH3),
44.8 (O=C-CH2), 47.6 (-C-CHO), 202.3 (-CHO), 205.1 (CH3- C=O);
Microanalysis calcd/found: C: 71.70 71.95; H: 10.94 10.77.
