$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Wacker-Type
Oxidation A two-necked flask equipped with a magnetic stirring bar and an
argon outlet is charged with Pd(OAc)2 (13.7 mg, 0.061 mmol), benzoquinone
(60 mg, 0.55 mmol) and CH3CN (7 mL). Water (7mL, CH3CN/H2O=7/1) and then
HClO4 (0.13 mL, 0.3 M) are successively added. The solution is vigorously
stirred for 1 h at 20°C and then the steroid (0.2 g, 0.61 mmol) is added.
When the reaction is over (TLC), the mixture is poured into a 30% aqueous
solution of NaOH. The extracts are filtered and then concentrated under
vacuum. The crude product is purified by chromatography on silica gel
(Et2O-petroleum ether). (±)-(8β ,9β ,14α )-N-Ethyl-2-methoxy-17α
-acetyl-11-azagona-1,3,5(10)-trien-13β -ol (16): (70% yield,.55%
conversion). IR (neat) 3447, 2941, 1609, 1265,1040, 742 cm-1; 1H NMR
(CDCl3) 7.09 (1H, d, J = 2.2 Hz), 6.98 (1H, d, J = 8.2 Hz), 6.65 (1H, dd,
J = 8.2, 2.2 Hz), 4.05 (1H, d, J = 5.3 Hz), 3.79 (3H, s), 3.15 (2H, q, J
= 7.0 Hz), 3.05 (1H, m), 2.72 (1H, 1/2AB, J = 11.3 Hz), 2.57 (1H, 1/2AB,
J = 11.3 Hz), 2.40 (3H, m), 2.05 (3H, s), 1.93 (2H, m), 1.70 (5H, m),
1.18 (3H, t, J = 7.0 Hz); 13C NMR (CDCl3) 209.8, 158.7, 141.2, 138.5,
131.5, 129.5, 113.3, 111.6, 81.3, 61.9, 60.9, 60.0, 55.5, 53.1, 51.9,
43.9, 34.6, 33.1, 25.5, 25.3, 24.9, 23.3, 16.8. Anal. calcd for
C21H29NO3: C, 73.44; H, 8.51. Found: C, 73.60; H, 8.34.
