$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for oxidation reactions with
Pd(MeCN)2Cl(NO2)/CuCl2 (method A) Pd(MeCN)2Cl(NO2) (0.05 eq) and CuCl2
(0.2 eq) were activated for 2h in tert-BuOH (0.4M) at 55ºC with an oxygen
filled balloon placed on top. The catalyst was cooled to 30ºC and the
substrate (1.0 eq) added. The reaction was stirred at 30ºC under oxygen
and monitored by GC MS. Full conversion was observed in most cases after
16h. EtOAc (10 mL) and H2O (10 mL) were added. The aqueous layer was
extracted with EtOAc (3 x 10 mL), the combined organic layers washed with
saturated aq. NaHCO3 solution and H2O, and dried over MgSO4. The solvent
was evaporated in vacuum. 3-(1,3-Dioxoisoindolin-2-yl)-4-methylhexanal
(2k) 3-(1,3-Dioxoisoindolin-2-yl)-3-methylbutanal (2l) The reaction was
completed after 2 days. Column Chromatography (pentane:EtOAc = 2:1) gave
the aldehyde as colourless oil (74%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ=1.77 (s,
6H; CH3), 3.18 (s, 2H; CH2), 7.66 (dd, 3 J=5.4 Hz, 4 J=3.0 Hz, 2H; CH),
7.76 (dd, 3 J=5.3 Hz, 4 J=3.2 Hz, 2H; CH), 9.78 (s, 1H; CHO). 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3): δ=27.7 (CH3), 53.0 (CH2), 57.1 (CH), 122.8 (CH), 131.8 (C),
133.9 (CH), 169.4 (CO), 199.5 (CHO). HR-ESI-MS: m/z calcd for C12H14NO3
[M+H]+ 232.0967, found 232.0968.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM selective for the aldehyde, Wacker oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Aldehyde Selective Wacker Oxidations of Phthalimide Protected Allylic
Amines: A New Catalytic Route to β3-Amino Acids
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
